;; D181 regression. The evaluator's core table takes core fn values inside
;; cached runtime code; `update` has the arity [m k f x y z & more], so its
;; value is a $FnV with k = 6 that only the runtime library ever lowers. A
;; restored library that forgot the session's var-k counter emitted a
;; dispatcher without the k = 6 branch, and this call reached `unreachable`
;; on every warm cache (fresh caches passed). run-corpus warms the cache
;; before it runs, so this program exercises the restored path.
(println (eval (quote (apply update {:a 1} :a + [1 2 3 4 5]))))
